<title>HUNGARY: Hungary BSE CEO Jozsef Rotyis says to step down.</title>
<headline>Hungary BSE CEO Jozsef Rotyis says to step down.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jozsef Rotyis, the CEO of the Budapest Stock Exchange said on Friday he would step down from his position in the autumn to take a new job.</p>
<p>&quot;My future work-place will be a credit rating agency,&quot; Rotyis told a news conference.</p>
<p>Zsigmond Jarai, chairman of the bourse's council, said the BSE would be inviting applications for a replacement for Rotyis.</p>
<p>-- Emese Bartha, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
